# Yanir's photograph. The image is public once the site renders it, so this is
# not about hiding his face - it is that this repository is public and git
# history is permanent. A personal photo committed here survives every fork and
# every clone, long after any decision to take it down.
#
# Production supplies it through VITE_AVATAR_URL instead, and the committed
# placeholder is the initial-letter mark the avatar falls back to, so a fresh
# clone renders correctly with no binary in the tree. See src/components/MessageAvatar.tsx.
/public/profile.jpeg
